module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.EtaleFundamental.GaloisCategoryAxioms
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.SpecializationSurjective
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Smooth.GeometricallyReducedFibres
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Algebra.Group.PrimeToPQuotient
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Specialization and the maximal prime-to-`p` quotient

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a smooth proper morphism with geometrically connected fibres, let `s' ⇝ s` be
a specialization of points of `S` and let `sp : π₁(X_{s̄'}) ⟶ π₁(X_{s̄})` be the resulting
specialization map. This file does two things.

Surjectivity of `sp` is unconditional at these hypotheses: a smooth morphism is flat and has
geometrically reduced fibres, so surjectivity for a flat proper morphism with one geometrically
reduced fibre applies verbatim.

For the maximal prime-to-`p` quotients `π'₁` the file supplies the reduction to a single
geometric input. Write `G' = π₁(X_{s̄'})` and `G = π₁(X_{s̄})`. An open normal subgroup
`N ≤ G'` of index prime to `p` is the stabilizer attached to a Galois finite étale cover of
`X_{s̄'}` whose Galois group `G'/N` has order prime to `p`. The input is that each such cover is
the base change of a finite étale cover of `X_A`, where `A` is the strict henselization of
`𝒪_{S,s}` used to build `sp`; in group-theoretic terms, that `N` is the preimage along `sp` of an
open normal subgroup `M ≤ G`. Granted that, `sp` induces an isomorphism
`π'₁(X_{s̄'}) ≅ π'₁(X_{s̄})` commuting with the projections: surjectivity comes from surjectivity
of `sp`, and injectivity from the descent of the prime-to-`p` quotients.

The prime-to-`p` condition on `M` is not part of the input. Because `sp` is surjective,
`M.index = (M.comap sp).index = N.index`, so it is automatic.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_specializationMap_of_smooth`: a specialization map of a smooth
  proper morphism with geometrically connected fibres is surjective, with no further hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_forall_lift`: both conclusions at
  once, the second one granted the descent of the prime-to-`p` finite quotients.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_isProP_ker`: the same, with the
  descent replaced by the hypothesis that the kernel of `sp` is pro-`p`, for `p` prime. This is
  the shape in which the input is usually described: the kernel of specialization is generated by
  wild inertia.

## Implementation notes

The descent input is stated on open normal subgroups of the étale fundamental group rather than
on finite étale covers. The two are interchangeable through the dictionary between open subgroups
of `π₁` and finite étale covers
(`AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleFundamentalGroup.IsOpenSubgroup`), and the subgroup form is the one the
group-theoretic argument consumes directly.

What is *not* proved here, and is the only thing standing between this file and Stacks Tag 0C0R,
is that input. The Stacks proof of it is the Noetherian approximation, reduction to a strictly
henselian discrete valuation ring, normalization, Abhyankar's lemma, purity of the branch locus
and henselian descent argument of Tag 0C0Q, restricted to Galois objects whose Galois group has
order prime to `p`; see the module documentation of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FundamentalGroup.SpecializationInjective.EssentiallySurjective`
for the characteristic-zero form of the same input, which is likewise carried there as a
hypothesis.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits IsLocalRing Stacks.FundamentalGroup

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- **Surjectivity of a specialization map in the smooth proper case.** Let `f : X ⟶ S` be smooth
and proper with geometrically connected fibres, let `s'` and `s` be geometric points of `S`, and
let `sp : π₁(X_{s̄'}) ⟶ π₁(X_{s̄})` be a specialization map. Then `sp` is surjective.

A smooth morphism is flat, and its fibres are geometrically reduced, so this is
`AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_isSpecializationMap_of_isProper_of_flat` with both of its remaining
hypotheses discharged. -/
@[sga "1 X 3.8" "more general"]
theorem surjective_specializationMap_of_smooth {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    [Smooth f] [IsProper f] [GeometricallyConnected f] (s' s : GeometricPoint S)
    (x' : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s'))
    (x : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s))
    (sp : EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x' →ₜ*
      EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x)
    (hsp : IsSpecializationMap f s' s x' x sp) :
    Function.Surjective sp := by
  have hgr : GeometricallyReduced f := geometricallyReduced_of_smooth f
  exact surjective_isSpecializationMap_of_isProper_of_flat f s' s inferInstance x' x sp hsp

/-- **Specialization is an isomorphism on maximal prime-to-`p` quotients, granted the descent of
the prime-to-`p` finite quotients.**

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be smooth and proper with geometrically connected fibres and let
`sp : π₁(X_{s̄'}) ⟶ π₁(X_{s̄})` be a specialization map. Suppose every open normal subgroup `N` of
`π₁(X_{s̄'})` of index prime to `p` is the preimage along `sp` of an open normal subgroup of
`π₁(X_{s̄})` — equivalently, every Galois finite étale cover of `X_{s̄'}` whose Galois group has
order prime to `p` descends. Then `sp` is surjective and induces an isomorphism of topological
groups `π'₁(X_{s̄'}) ≅ π'₁(X_{s̄})` of the maximal prime-to-`p` quotients, commuting with the
projections.

Surjectivity is `AlgebraicGeometry.surjective_specializationMap_of_smooth` and needs no
hypothesis beyond smoothness and properness; the isomorphism is
`Stacks.FundamentalGroup.exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP`, whose compactness requirement is
met because the étale fundamental group is profinite. -/
theorem exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_forall_lift {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    [Smooth f] [IsProper f] [GeometricallyConnected f] (s' s : GeometricPoint S) (p : ℕ)
    (x' : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s'))
    (x : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s))
    (sp : EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x' →ₜ*
      EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x)
    (hsp : IsSpecializationMap f s' s x' x sp)
    (hlift : ∀ N : Subgroup (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x'),
      N.Normal → IsOpen (N : Set (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x')) →
      ¬ p ∣ N.index →
      ∃ M : Subgroup (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x),
        M.Normal ∧ IsOpen (M : Set (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x)) ∧
          M.comap sp.toMonoidHom = N) :
    Function.Surjective sp ∧
      ∃ e : PrimeToP p (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x') ≃ₜ*
          PrimeToP p (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x),
        ∀ g, e (primeToPMk p _ g) = primeToPMk p _ (sp g) := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective sp :=
    surjective_specializationMap_of_smooth f s' s x' x sp hsp
  let : CompactSpace (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x') :=
    compactSpace_etaleFundamentalGroup _ x'
  exact ⟨hsurj, exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP sp hsurj hlift⟩

/-- **Specialization is an isomorphism on maximal prime-to-`p` quotients when its kernel is
pro-`p`.**

For `p` prime, a pro-`p` subgroup meets every finite quotient of order prime to `p` trivially, so
a pro-`p` kernel is contained in every open normal subgroup of index prime to `p`. That makes the
descent hypothesis of
`AlgebraicGeometry.exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_forall_lift` automatic: an open normal
`N` of index prime to `p` contains the kernel, hence is the preimage of its own image. -/
theorem exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_isProP_ker {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)
    [Smooth f] [IsProper f] [GeometricallyConnected f] (s' s : GeometricPoint S) {p : ℕ}
    (hp : p.Prime)
    (x' : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s'))
    (x : GeometricPoint (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s))
    (sp : EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x' →ₜ*
      EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x)
    (hsp : IsSpecializationMap f s' s x' x sp)
    (hker : IsProP p ↥(MonoidHom.ker sp.toMonoidHom)) :
    Function.Surjective sp ∧
      ∃ e : PrimeToP p (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s') x') ≃ₜ*
          PrimeToP p (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x),
        ∀ g, e (primeToPMk p _ g) = primeToPMk p _ (sp g) := by
  have hsurj : Function.Surjective sp :=
    surjective_specializationMap_of_smooth f s' s x' x sp hsp
  let : T2Space (EtaleFundamentalGroup (fiberOverGeometricPoint f s) x) :=
    t2Space_etaleFundamentalGroup _ x
  exact exists_continuousMulEquiv_primeToP_of_forall_lift f s' s p x' x sp hsp
    (forall_lift_of_isProP_ker hp sp hsurj hker)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
